session:pr630Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #47 (query-builder Phase 4, docs/plans/QUERY_BUILDER_PLAN.md) asked to replace the horizontal flex-row node-card layout in the visual query builder (sparql_endpoint/src/frontend.html, /?view=build) with a Cytoscape.js graph, using cytoscape-node-html-label (or styled boxes as fallback) if the plugin worked cleanly. Checked provenance for prior Cytoscape-integration work in this file (PR #255: the query-result graph view's drag/save-layout pattern) and reused its instance-lifecycle convention — renderQbNodeCanvas keeps its own qbCyInstance global, destroyed and rebuilt from scratch on every render, mirroring the existing cyInstance/classCyInstance pattern rather than trying to diff/patch the graph. Confirmed cytoscape-node-html-label@1.2.2 is reachable on jsdelivr and inspected its ~2KB source directly (curl) before committing to it, since the plan doc flagged 'fall back to styled boxes' as the decision point if the plugin added complexity — it turned out to be a clean self-registering UMD bundle, so the plugin path was taken. The QueryNode tree is flattened by a DFS walk into cytoscape nodes/edges (node id = the already-unique varName), laid out left-to-right with the already-loaded cytoscape-dagre extension (reused verbatim, not reimplemented) to preserve the original layout's left-to-right reading order. Card click-to-activate and remove-node are wired through one delegated click listener on #node-canvas (matched via e.target.closest against data-var attributes) rather than per-card DOM listeners, since the html-label overlay divs are fully torn down and recreated on every render — per-card listeners would need re-attaching every time anyway, so delegation removes that bookkeeping. The .node-card/.node-var/.btn-remove-node markup and CSS classes were deliberately kept identical to the old implementation so the existing Selenium/thirtyfour tests in sparql_endpoint/tests/frontend_browser.rs (#node-canvas .node-card, .btn-remove-node, active-class assertions) kept working unmodified against the new rendering path. Verified end-to-end in a real headless-shell browser (no geckodriver/firefox available in this sandboxed worktree environment, and no root to apt-get one in; downloaded Chrome for Testing via `npx playwright install chromium` and manually extracted the missing shared libs — libnspr4/libnss3/libxres1/etc — from `apt-get download` .deb packages into a local prefix via LD_LIBRARY_PATH, since apt itself needed root): selecting a class renders one node card, following an object property adds a second node plus a labelled edge (cytoscape reports node/edge counts matching), clicking the second card sets it active, and the remove button shrinks the graph back down, with zero console/page errors. That same manual check caught a real layout bug the automated tests couldn't (long/unprefixed class IRIs have no max-width constraint in flex layout, so the .node-card div grew past the Cytoscape node's assigned 170x64 bounding box and visually overlapped its neighbor) — fixed by giving .node-card a fixed width matching the node style's width and adding overflow-wrap, plus bumping the node box height for a two-line title, in a follow-up commit." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:630 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr630 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
